# Warpdrive: independent email and Iranian integrations

**Status: APPROVED by Ali on 31 October 2026 for P0 and P1 with the stated defaults. Implementation starts with non-Gmail email.**

Prepared 31 October 2026. Inspected source: `main` at `8539fe8c4aeb0b58b6d05e629710460ef90bbed4`. Market context: the supplied Iranian CRM research snapshot. Priorities below are proposed product decisions, not verified customer demand or promises of provider availability.

## 1. Summary

Extend Warpdrive so teams can use independent business email and Iranian communication/accounting services through complete, secure workflows. Deliver generic email and the first Iranian SMS integration first, preserving the current application design and complete Farsi, German and English support. Validate the resulting sales workflow with pilots before broadening the platform.

**Proposed approval scope:** implement P0, then P1 in the order below, respecting dependencies and provider qualification gates. P2 is a deferred backlog requiring a later scope decision. Approval permits development, migration rehearsals and isolated contract tests; connecting real customer accounts, sending messages, placing calls, posting financial documents or starting paid services requires explicit authorization for those actions. No purchases or external communications are part of preparing this plan.

## Coordination amendment, 31 October 2026

The master integration programme and this approved P0/P1 slice use one ownership/task map, recorded in `integration-coordination.md`. Shared CONN owns the registry, credentials, connection lifecycle and hub; EVT owns common delivery and rules. MAIL owns mail-domain changes; MS owns the single Outlook adapter; EXP-041..048 own the selected PBX/accounting tracks. Existing work must be reconciled under BASE, never reset or rebuilt in parallel.

Independent email remains first at P0. The initial qualified SMS provider follows; the remaining approved P1 work is followed by as many independently verifiable SMS providers as practical. Kavenegar and Melipayamak remain initial/default candidates, not the entire provider scope. A dated 30-candidate inventory and independent stage tasks are maintained in the master register. Unverifiable candidates are excluded or remain pending, never advertised as supported. Complete FA/DE/EN workflows and existing UI/auth/security requirements remain unchanged.

The original IG IDs remain scope cross-references rather than duplicate implementation issues. The master register records priority exceptions: early MAIL is P0; the mail-only Microsoft path need not wait for calendar; selected PBX/accounting tracks are P1 rather than the earlier generic P3 backlog. This documentation update does not activate or alter persistent-goal state, start new implementation or authorize live actions.

## 2. Ownership and decisions

| Owner                    | Responsibility                                                                                                                                  |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Ali                      | Approve scope/defaults, choose pilot customers, authorize real provider access and live actions, accept release workflows.                      |
| Implementing maintainers | Design and deliver the approved increments, preserve peer work, capture test evidence, surface provider limitations and material scope changes. |

Routine implementation choices stay within this approved scope. Unsupported APIs, changed commercial terms or a substantially different workflow return as a concrete decision; they do not justify silently reducing functionality or introducing another vendor dependency.

## 3. Current state and gaps

- Better Auth is merged. Independent application login and independent SMTP for authentication notices already exist. Customer mailbox synchronization remains Gmail-based; authentication SMTP is not a customer mailbox connector.
- Email storage currently permits one account per user and carries Gmail-specific message, thread, cursor and attachment identifiers. The current Gmail first sync starts from connection time, without historical backfill. These constraints require an additive migration and a provider-neutral mail domain.
- Reuse the existing encrypted credentials, durable send outbox, job leases, retry/reconciliation states, visibility checks and auth offboarding. Extend their coverage to each provider instead of creating a parallel security model.
- Connected Apps currently lists OAuth/MCP client grants. It is not a third-party connector installation catalog. Preserve those grants while adding an understandable integration setup and management entry point.
- Iranian SMS, PBX and accounting connectors were not established in the inspected source. Partial multi-currency support exists; the README still incorrectly labels it entirely out of scope. Exchange-rate conversion is absent.
- The market snapshot is useful discovery evidence. It does not establish customer demand, competitor implementation quality, market share or a complete national supplier count. Product claims need commit-pinned evidence and provider-tested qualification.

## 4. Objectives and measurable release results

Customer outcome: complete daily sales follow-up using chosen email, phone and SMS services while retaining control of CRM data. Business outcome: learn which complete workflow makes a pilot team adopt and continue using Warpdrive.

| Result                     | Baseline                                       | Proposed acceptance point                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Independent email          | No non-Gmail customer mailbox adapter          | By P0 acceptance, complete the workflow on a clean self-hosted IMAP/SMTP installation and one separately authorized external mailbox service; preserve Gmail regression coverage.                                                                                        |
| Iranian communication      | No qualified Iranian SMS adapter               | By P0 acceptance, one qualified provider supports send, receipt tracking and inbound reconciliation using approved test numbers; provider-specific limits are documented.                                                                                                |
| Localization and authority | Existing FA/DE/EN design and permission system | At every increment, zero unlocalized new states in the reviewed workflow matrix and zero known permission bypasses in the agreed negative tests.                                                                                                                         |
| Adoption learning          | No verified pilot baseline supplied            | During the P1 pilot tranche, target five organizations across at least two industries, record task completion and retention, and compare follow-up effort against each team's measured baseline. This is learning evidence, not statistical proof of product-market fit. |

No calendar delivery dates or measured customer-performance improvements are assumed. Sizes indicate relative complexity; timing follows the first technical qualification and actual provider access.

## 5. Initial users

1. **Independent-mail sales teams:** people who need customer communication inside the CRM while their organization uses its own mail server or a non-Google mail service.
2. **Iranian operational sales teams:** people who need incoming leads, local calls/SMS, quotations and accounting handoff connected to customer records.
3. **Multilingual operators:** people who need to work naturally in Farsi or German while serving customers whose language, calendar and currency preferences may differ from their own.

Industry and willingness-to-pay assumptions remain open until pilot discovery. German support is a product requirement across these workflows, not a claim that an Iran-specific connector must serve German providers.

## 6. Value and scope choices

| Need                           | Proposed investment                                                                          | Evidence still needed                                                             |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Control and independent access | Self-hosted core workflow, independent mail, usable export/restore                           | Repeatable installation and operation in approved target hosting.                 |
| Natural local operations       | Strong Farsi/German UX, Iranian data handling, SMS/PBX/accounting links                      | Real provider/account compatibility and actual user task completion.              |
| Trustworthy integrations       | Explicit ownership, permissions, delivery status, audit and recoverable failures             | Negative, concurrency, outage and offboarding tests for every connector.          |
| Competitive breadth            | Complete the first sales workflow; retain broader service/automation/marketplace items in P2 | Identified switching reasons from interviews and identical-scenario vendor demos. |

This positioning is a hypothesis. Open source, localization and MCP do not individually establish a unique advantage.

## 7. Prioritized delivery tasks

P0 covers four capabilities: independent email, reusable connection management, Iranian SMS/data handling, and localized acceptance. P1 completes the first operational workflow. Farsi/German work and security are required within every task, never postponed to the end.

Size: S = contained; M = several related surfaces; L = substantial integration; XL = substantial integration with unresolved external dependencies. These are not duration estimates.

